>>
Rule 1 (tensor must be 2-dimensional to avoid ValueError)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 2
>>
Rule 2 (non-empty 2D tensor for a meaningful identity initialization)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 2 then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0
>>
Rule 3 (tensor has a well-defined dtype)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = dtype_(v_1)
>>
Rule 4 (union-typed tensor parameter is still required to be 2D)
{v_1 : tensor ⊎ tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 2
